# text = They have got possession of the land, or the city, of Zarahemla; they have appointed a king over them, and he hath written unto the king of the Lamanites, in the which he hath joined an alliance with him; in the which alliance he hath agreed to maintain the city of Zarahemla, which maintenance he supposeth will enable the Lamanites to conquer the remainder of the land, and he shall be placed king over this people when they shall be conquered under the Lamanites.
# sent_id = 2375
# llm_note = Long complex sentence. Multiple semicolon-joined coordinate clauses sharing subject "they/he". "got possession of the land, or the city, of Zarahemla" = root clause; "or the city" = appos of "land". "in the which" = archaic relative prepositional phrase (fused relative); treat "which" as relcl on antecedent "Lamanites". "which maintenance he supposeth will enable" = relcl on "city of Zarahemla"; "supposeth" = cognition verb + ccomp ("will enable..."); "enable the Lamanites to conquer" = causative xcomp. "he shall be placed king" = passive + xcomp "king". "when they shall be conquered" = advcl temporal.
